  "reproduce": "set -a; . ./.dev.vars; set +a; npm run ablate -- \"<task>\" --input=\"<fixed input>\" --pairs=3",
  "method": "One warm-up run populates task memory. That snapshot is then frozen and every arm reads it, so no arm can learn from another. Arms alternate memory-on/memory-off over the same fixed input and the same starting graph, one at a time. Tool-free, so no app authorization is involved and the only variable is memory.",
  "limits": [
    "One task, one input, three runs per arm. Directional only; not a significance test.",
    "A rubric score is a judged result against this task's frozen checks, not measured accuracy.",
    "Tool-free: this measures task memory, not the cross-task tool-knowledge store.",
    "An earlier run of this same harness without the warm-up returned memory_hurt at n=3. That run was invalid: the snapshot was empty, so both arms were identical and it measured model variance. Retained here as the reason the warm-up and the empty-memory guard exist."
  ]
